  "title": "A dataset recording joint EEG-fMRI during affective music listening ",
  "description": "Joint EEG-fMRI recordings from 21 healthy adults who listened to music stimuli chosen and generated to evoke different affective responses. Participants self-reported their felt affective states during listening. The dataset supports research on the neural correlates of emotional responses to music, including sub-cortical activity reflected in EEG.",
  "methods_description": "Simultaneous EEG and fMRI were recorded from 21 healthy adult participants in 2016 while they listened to affective music stimuli. Participants self-reported their felt affective states as they listened.",
